  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The current best (config_045: 0.713 acc) uses resnet50 as the image encoder in a multiprofile + transformer + weighted fusion setting. The only prior evidence on image encoder choice comes from singleprofile experiments (config_016 resnet50: 0.540 vs config_051 imagenet_vit_l: 0.537), where the difference was small and the regime was fundamentally different (no multiprofile aggregation). config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_045, isolating the effect of image encoder in the high-performing multiprofile + transformer regime. This is critical because the image encoder determines the quality of the visual representation being fused, and confirming whether resnet50's advantage persists (or reverses) when paired with transformer aggregation will guide all subsequent multimodal experiments. Under the limited budget, this is the highest-information exploitation step: it either validates the current best's encoder choice (allowing us to fix that variable) or reveals a better encoder that could push performance further."
}

